                <pb facs="0279" n="161" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg161"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">314.115C43/179: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Geissler</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-02T15:00:00-05:00">November 2, 1929—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>65. Your 141 of October 31. Department agrees in substance to proposal of
                    Guatemalan Government but considers the name of the arbitrator should appear and
                    that the passage in question should read as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p rendition="#flush">“it is agreed by the two governments that this
                            question shall be submitted to Sir Herbert Sisnett, Chief Justice of
                            British Honduras as arbitrator. The question to be submitted to the
                            arbitrator is as follows.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
